>> title: Cornbread
>> part: Baking

Skillet cornbread based on a recipe by Kenji López-Alt [^https://www.seriouseats.com/moist-and-tender-brown-butter-cornbread-recipe].

= Recipe

Add butter to a 10-inch skillet and place in {{425%°F}} oven until melted and slightly browned.

@unsalted butter{7%tbsp}

In a mixing bowl, add yellow cornmeal, flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, and sugar.

@fine yellow cornmeal{130%g|1%cup}
@all-purpose flour{130%g|1%cup}
@sugar{50%g|4%tbsp}
@baking powder{2%tsp}
@kosher salt{1%tsp}
@baking soda{1/4%tsp}

Transfer the browned butter back to the mixing bowl and add eggs, buttermilk, and sour cream.

@eggs{2}
@sour cream{170%g|3/4%cup}
@cultured buttermilk{113%g|1/2%cup}

Whisk together and pour into the hot cast iron skillet coated with the remnants of the browned butter. Bake until cooked through and browned, about 20 to 25 minutes.
